The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
// SMCR_EL1 and SMPRI_EL1 reset to an architecturally UNKNOWN value on suspend exit.
write_sysreg_s(0, SYS_SMPRI_EL1);
```
Reason:
The registers SMCR_EL1 and SMPRI_EL1 do not retain their configured values when the system exits suspend mode, resulting in a loss of any traps that were previously set. This leads to misconfiguration of the SME state upon resuming, as the system does not restore the necessary settings.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
u64 smcr = 0;
if (system_supports_fa64())
    smcr |= SMCR_ELx_FA64;
write_sysreg_s(smcr, SYS_SMCR_EL1);
```
Reason:
The patch initializes the SMCR_EL1 register with the appropriate configuration (including the FA64 setting if supported) upon exiting suspend. This ensures that the necessary traps are correctly restored, preventing misconfiguration of the SME state when the system resumes.

